      <activity id="8f649022-57d3-5534-86d9-ec101e5bde11" activityNameId="6ac1819b-be8e-5a5e-b58a-d407d64a3956" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Expanded perlite, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Expanded perlite, at plant
Expanded by shock heating at a temperature of 870 – 1090 °C. It is assumed that light fuel oil is used for heating. Density of expanded perlite: 60 - 300kg/m3 ;
UUID: cc5a5489-57b7-3a3a-82a4-9c30825778e9
includes the raw material, the transport to the finishing plant and some internal transports, the heating energy carrier, some packaging materials, the infrastructure and the emissions
Location: For some exchanges CH, RER and OCE modules have been used as proxy.
Technology: Basic principle is a heating of the perlite grains to high temperature. The volume increase is 15 – 30 fold
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: See geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cc5a5489-57b7-3a3a-82a4-9c30825778e9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
